WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.234
And what you make of

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.502
how Republicans on Capitol Hill

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.338
today were responding to that 70 minutes

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.406
last night.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.008
I'm actually impressed that they

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:08.975
that a number of them

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.210
responded the way they did.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:10.777
I mean, first off,

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.945
I thought you did a great job.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.646
I mean, I think you did

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:14.047
the best

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.182
job anybody could expect out of anybody

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.018
going up against Donald Trump.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.086
I mean, it was to your point last door,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.287
I guess, by the way,

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:23.289
he said that behind your back

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.457
was over there.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.358
But to your point

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.260
last night that you made it was a rerun.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.062
I mean, this was Trump

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.297
being Trump, as he's always been.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:34.167
And I'm disappointed that we didn't see

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.836
something new, like just put everything

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.306
that happened on 20, 20 the trial.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.741
There's ways to deflect that

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.410
and put it in the rearview mirror.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.744
But tell us what we're going to do next.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.112
So I'm actually very impressed

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.847
that we had Republicans on the Hill

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.249
that were willing to at least address

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:49.816
the issue.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.550
Now, there were some

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.185
that just don't want to even get involved

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.853
in the noise, like Lisa Murkowski,

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.688
who's from my home state.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:56.589
I commend her for that.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:57.957
I mean, at least

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.126
let the noise die down and then come out

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.561
and make a statement later

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.629
when she has to them.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:03.930
Ben, what do you think?

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.531
Well,

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:04.931
first of all,

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.633
I just appreciated you

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.268
being the matador against the bull

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:10.804
Anybody who's got a conversation

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:11.805
with Donald Trump knows

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.940
it is a very hard thing to do, just even,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.175
you know, in normal life,

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.776
let alone in front of millions of people.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.245
And I also thought it was a rerun.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.346
It was a repeat.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.915
But I think you also

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:22.849
put him in a position

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.818
where he revealed some things

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:25.952
that people who don't watch him

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.120
all the time were not aware of.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:27.487
For instance,

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.755
he's updated

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.990
his sort of weaponizing, of nostalgia

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.158
before it was Make America

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.027
Great Again from the fifties.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.228
And that's very appealing

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:36.529
to people who feel that

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.231
today is a rough period.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.632
He's now moved it up.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.101
No, Make America Great Again.

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.302
Just two years ago.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.870
Just two years ago. It was great.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.872
It was perfect. Everything was wonderful.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.340
And if he stays there,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.442
where he's praising his own past

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:50.610
and point to the future

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.512
and sticks Biden with the president,

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:53.379
that's dangerous.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.415
And so I think now Democrats

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.616
now have a chance to look at it.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.517
We can start getting ready.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.451
We can see a little bit

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.719
of how he's going to move.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:00.920
And I think a lot of Democrats

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.722
had not watched him for three years.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.824
Shocking how how terrible he still is.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:05.391
But also,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.993
you see that the virus is mutating

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.595
and we've got to be ready for him.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:09.929
What did you think?

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.564
Especially given obviously

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.365
one of his arguments

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.233
he's been making lately

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.567
is that maybe he won't participate

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.969
in the Republican primary debates

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.670
because he is so far ahead

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.205
currently in the polls.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.573
But he didn't spend a lot of time

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:21.040
last night

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.742
talking about Biden or his record.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.010
Now, I was very struck by that.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.712
And I just want to echo everyone else.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.646
He tried repeatedly

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.914
to get under your skin.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:28.781
You never let him.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:29.883
And it was a real reminder

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:31.084
of the briefing room

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.485
version of you that we saw

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.186
over many years.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.223
I think that he was lucky.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.392
He went in there and I had been hearing

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.894
and my colleagues have been hearing,

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.162
you know, there's going to start

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.997
being a sort of a pivot more toward Biden

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:44.430
that that's

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.999
where the energy is going to be.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.467
You know, he's essentially running

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.402
as a as an incumbent, Donald Trump.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.370
And so, you know,

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.438
he there isn't really a Republican field.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.506
He doesn't want to give

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.707
those challengers.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.709
He he can't stop defending himself

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:57.710
or talking about himself.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.945
And so, consequently,

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.246
he's spent almost no time

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.281
talking about Biden.

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:02.382
It was very little.

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.118
You know, that will be a problem for him.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:06.920
And that is his problem,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.121
you know, for years

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.656
is that he wants to talk about himself

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.724
and the past Van's point.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:12.358
You know,

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.626
I think that his folks

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.462
still feel good about the contrast

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:17.797
that he can show

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.933
or they think he can show with Biden

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:22.101
in terms of doing a format like that.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.169
I think they still think

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:24.571
that he is going to be able

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.072
to try to appear

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.473
dominant or strong

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:28.107
and he's going to try

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:30.710
to draw a weakness contrast with Biden.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:31.844
You know, again,

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.413
this primary is not over.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.147
We should not

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:36.082
suggest that he's a nominee.

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.650
But I think that's where they're going

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.685
to be looking.

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:40.186
What I also was struck by,

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.754
he cannot help himself on

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:42.522
wanting to mix it up

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.957
and wanting to be on stage.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:44.991
And so yes,

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.392
I understand that he's been doing

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:47.760
a lot of I'm not going to debate.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.529
I do think there's a real chance he skips

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.464
at least one and maybe two.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:52.031
Very hard for me

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:52.632
to imagine him

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.100
seeing a bunch of Republicans on stage

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.935
talking about him and him,

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:56.703
you know, saying, yeah,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.604
you know what, I'm going to I'm

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:58.938
going to sit this one out.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:03:59.305
Yeah.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:03:59.572
David,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.641
what's your sense of how Republicans

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.676
are responding to what you saw today?

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.544
And also,

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:04.777
you know,

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:05.778
the fact that the White House,

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:06.145
you know,

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.013
immediately was like,

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.348
you want four more years of this,

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:09.782
they're fundraising off of it.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.184
Well, look, to to Van's

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:12.752
point on your last point,

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:13.353
you know,

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.220
a lot of Americans

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:14.821
don't share

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.122
this halcyon view

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.857
of what those years were like.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.826
Those years were chaotic.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.628
They were exhausting.

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:24.697
And, you know, the more you see of Trump,

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.132
as we saw him last night,

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.734
the more it brings that back.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.836
So I think that strategically was smart

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:31.304
of them to do it.

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:31.638
In terms

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:33.573
of how the Republicans reacted

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:36.242
I do think just as a reality check,

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.211
they reacted the way they did

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:40.313
because as they have been for years,

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.548
they're fearful of Trump's base,

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.317
which is the dominant force

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.352
in Republican politics today.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.454
And he is, in fact, a

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.157
I think, a fairly substantial frontrunner

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:51.991
in this race.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:52.759
There are a lot of

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:54.294
Republicans who share other views

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.529
who wish that weren't so.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.131
But you heard it in that room.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.065
You know, people say, well,

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.533
it sounds like a Trump rally

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:01.467
sound like a Trump rally

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:04.137
because you at CNN assembled

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.673
a representative group of Republicans

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:07.440
in New Hampshire.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.342
He's at 50% in the polls

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:10.209
in New Hampshire.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.412
The governor of the state has had 11

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:13.579
In those same polls,

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:16.382
he is in a dominant position.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.051
So that what you saw were

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.018
a lot of politicians

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.087
who just didn't want to deal with it

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.755
and didn't want to comment on it.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.325
Some of them who ducked into hallways.

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.959
And I hate to be a man who

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.262
raised eyebrows you who must feel like,

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:30.430
you know,

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.030
like he's

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.032
carrying the plague or something

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.500
because every time he

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.068
I think we'll see him

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:35.868
with a microphone

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.470
that go into a door

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.372
and slam the door shut.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:40.740
But they don't want to talk about it

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.141
because they don't want to offend

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:42.975
his base.

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:43.743
And one of the things

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.345
his opponents are going to have to decide

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.512
is, I mean,

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.880
are they going to continue

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.082
to play that game?

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.383
I saw Tim Scott running

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:51.984
into one of those doors

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:54.053
are you going to continue to let him,

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:55.788
you know,

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.423
behave outrageously

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.092
and have nothing to say about it?

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:00.960
Is that really a winning formula?

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.662
If you're running for president?

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:03.930
I would actually just

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:04.297
I don't

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.431
I think there is some element

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.332
of what you're saying there.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.401
But I recall back in 20, 15,

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:10.169
the same thing was going on.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.971
He said they went out with Dr.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.373
Carson's campaign

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:14.774
and everybody wanted to talk about

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:16.442
what Trump was doing.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.310
And they would ask

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.112
every single one of the eight of us

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.613
that were on the ballot at the time

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.848
and they would ask people on the Hill,

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.282
What do you think about Trump now

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.117
at the time?

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:25.418
The stock answer was,

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:26.152
There is no way

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:27.687
this guy is going to win the primary.

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:28.354
Right.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.423
That we cannot put up with this

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.657
let's talk about serious issues.

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:34.193
So I think to some extent, some of these

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:34.994
members now,

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:36.696
you know, you showed

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:37.764
a sample clipping

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:38.898
of some of the members they talked to.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.633
I don't know how many overall mean

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:41.534
he talked to overall,

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:43.503
but I think there is some element of,

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.771
look, we've got serious business

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:46.439
that we have to deal with right now.

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.373
That's the last thing

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:48.841
that I want to be talking about.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.343
But the problem is, is it's

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:50.777
the last thing

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:51.878
that they want to be talking about,

00:06:51.878 --> 00:06:53.312
I think in large measure,

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:54.814
because there's nothing great to say.

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:56.749
And what I was very struck by today,

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:57.617
two things.

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:58.718
The volume of headlines

00:06:58.718 --> 00:06:59.585
that you just showed

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:00.119
it just speaks

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:00.453
to how much

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:01.988
news came out of this town hall.

00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:03.222
And I think it was important

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:04.390
for people to hear

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:05.825
where he is on positions

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:06.826
as opposed to just

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:08.127
the small groups of reporters

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.662
who are on the plane with him.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:10.263
Or, you know,

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:12.131
the occasional Newsmax interview

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:13.800
that he does or what have you.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.034
So, number one, that was important.

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:15.501
Number two,

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:16.269
I was really struck

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:17.236
by the number of people

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.604
who didn't want to say anything,

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:20.239
who have been more vocal

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:21.174
in recent months,

00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:23.242
who had been speaking out about Trump,

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:25.545
but didn't today and didn't last night,

00:07:25.745 --> 00:07:26.879
because I do think that's

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.915
a mark of his strength in this primary.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:29.882
They see him as heading

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.250
in a certain direction.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.453
I think it's a wake up call.

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:36.322
People have been very critical of CNN.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:37.523
How can you platform this?

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.025
How can you do this?

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:40.660
This thing is happening.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:42.995
Donald Trump is back and he is real.

